(Ti plant, asparagus family)
need to grow in the shade.

860
00:34:39,120 --> 00:34:40,720
They need indirect sunlight.

861
00:34:40,720 --> 00:34:42,680
The red acts like sunscreen.

862
00:34:42,680 --> 00:34:44,960
It turns chlorophyll into anthocyanins.

863
00:34:46,140 --> 00:34:47,920
(Grabs it)
Is this poisonous?

864
00:34:48,000 --> 00:34:48,380
Yes.

865
00:34:49,640 --> 00:34:50,880
But it's safe to touch!

866
00:34:50,940 --> 00:34:52,360
Just don't chew it.

867
00:34:52,360 --> 00:34:53,240
Don't eat it.

868
00:34:53,240 --> 00:34:53,840
The second he heard "poisonous",

869
00:34:53,840 --> 00:34:55,000
Bing started picking leaves

870
00:34:55,000 --> 00:34:56,600
to cook for us tonight!

871
00:34:56,680 --> 00:34:57,820
Poisonous? I'll take seven.

872
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:01,640
It feels like

873
00:35:01,640 --> 00:35:03,320
we signed up for a senior tour.

874
00:35:03,400 --> 00:35:04,230
A senior tour!

875
00:35:05,040 --> 00:35:05,920
It really feels like one.

876
00:35:05,920 --> 00:35:07,890
It's like seeing our future selves.

877
00:35:08,560 --> 00:35:09,830
And over here,

878
00:35:10,680 --> 00:35:13,510
(Fruit station)
let's try some rainforest fruits.

879
00:35:15,120 --> 00:35:16,360
But today's fruit tasting

880
00:35:16,360 --> 00:35:17,600
is a little different.

881
00:35:17,600 --> 00:35:19,560
Who likes sour stuff?

882
00:35:19,560 --> 00:35:20,480
I can handle sour.

883
00:35:20,480 --> 00:35:20,980
Okay.

884
00:35:20,980 --> 00:35:22,540
(Tangerines and lemons)

885
00:35:22,600 --> 00:35:23,960
This one's the sourest.

886
00:35:23,960 --> 00:35:24,840
(Sourness ranking: Strong to mild)
This one's next.

887
00:35:24,840 --> 00:35:25,680
This one's the least sour.

888
00:35:25,680 --> 00:35:26,760
Which one will you try?

889
00:35:26,760 --> 00:35:27,920
Don't eat this one yet.

890
00:35:27,920 --> 00:35:28,480
I'll try one.

891
00:35:32,540 --> 00:35:33,380
(So sour)

892
00:35:35,540 --> 00:35:37,420
(So sour)

893
00:35:39,860 --> 00:35:40,860
(So sour)

894
00:35:41,480 --> 00:35:43,000
(So sour)
It's not bad, right?

895
00:35:43,240 --> 00:35:44,240
I don't even wanna try it.

896
00:35:44,240 --> 00:35:45,200
Just hearing them chew

897
00:35:45,200 --> 00:35:46,680
makes my stomach turn.

898
00:35:46,760 --> 00:35:47,730
Might as well try one.

899
00:35:52,440 --> 00:35:53,600
And this one

900
00:35:53,600 --> 00:35:56,380
is a little berry from the rainforest.

901
00:35:56,760 --> 00:35:59,160
Is this the one
that changes how things taste?

902
00:35:59,160 --> 00:36:00,200
Yes.

903
00:36:00,280 --> 00:36:02,320
It makes sour foods taste sweet.

904
00:36:02,400 --> 00:36:03,160
Seriously?

905
00:36:03,160 --> 00:36:04,000
Seriously.

906
00:36:04,080 --> 00:36:05,030
The effect lasts a while.

907
00:36:06,360 --> 00:36:07,260
It really is sweet now!

908
00:36:07,260 --> 00:36:08,700
(Taste testing)

909
00:36:13,800 --> 00:36:14,520
It really is!

910
00:36:15,200 --> 00:36:15,920
That's amazing!

911
00:36:16,600 --> 00:36:18,020
It's super sweet.

912
00:36:18,560 --> 00:36:21,570
This fruit is called a miracle berry.

913
00:36:21,700 --> 00:36:22,720
(Miracle berry, native
to West African rainforests)

914
00:36:22,720 --> 00:36:24,090
(Contains miraculin, a glycoprotein)
It suppresses our

915
00:36:24,100 --> 00:36:25,280
(Sour foods taste sweet after eating it)
sour taste receptors.

916
00:36:25,280 --> 00:36:26,520
Since the fruit is red,

917
00:36:26,520 --> 00:36:27,840
it attracts birds to spread its seeds.

918
00:36:27,840 --> 00:36:28,840
But that's not enough.

919
00:36:28,840 --> 00:36:30,800
It wants mammals to spread them too.

920
00:36:30,800 --> 00:36:33,280
But it's neither fragrant nor sweet.

921
00:36:33,280 --> 00:36:34,640
So it evolved

922
00:36:34,640 --> 00:36:35,960
a special protein

923
00:36:35,960 --> 00:36:37,440
that makes sour foods

924
00:36:37,440 --> 00:36:38,840
taste sweet to mammals.

925
00:36:38,840 --> 00:36:39,680
I never knew that

926
00:36:39,680 --> 00:36:41,490
plants are so sneaky.

927
00:36:43,560 --> 00:36:44,240
And that wraps up

928
00:36:44,240 --> 00:36:45,800
today's activities.

929
00:36:45,800 --> 00:36:46,360
Awesome.

930
00:36:46,360 --> 00:36:47,600
That was nice.

931
00:36:47,680 --> 00:36:48,880
Time to cook!

932
00:36:48,880 --> 00:36:50,760
This rainforest's pretty cool.

933
00:36:50,840 --> 00:36:51,420
That was fun.

934
00:36:52,680 --> 00:36:53,820
That berry...

935
00:36:55,880 --> 00:36:58,520
really makes
everything sour taste sweet.

936
00:36:58,520 --> 00:37:00,000
How does that even work?

937
00:37:00,080 --> 00:37:02,280
Nature's pretty amazing.

938
00:37:02,360 --> 00:37:03,380
It really is nice.

939
00:37:04,080 --> 00:37:04,620
Cooling.

940
00:37:08,560 --> 00:37:09,640
I just got back from a rainforest.

941
00:37:09,640 --> 00:37:11,680
I spent over 100 days there.

942
00:37:12,040 --> 00:37:13,610
Right, filming that TV drama.

943
00:37:14,280 --> 00:37:15,770
Didn't you also visit

944
00:37:16,480 --> 00:37:17,760
a rainforest in South America?

945
00:37:18,000 --> 00:37:19,520
That rainforest

946
00:37:19,520 --> 00:37:22,320
covers this part of South America.

947
00:37:22,320 --> 00:37:24,720
It actually stretches across

948
00:37:24,720 --> 00:37:26,520
several countries.

949
00:37:26,600 --> 00:37:27,240
They share it.

950
00:37:27,240 --> 00:37:28,560
Right, they share it.

951
00:37:28,640 --> 00:37:30,240
Anyu, you don't even need books.

952
00:37:30,240 --> 00:37:31,440
Just talk to Hu more.

953
00:37:31,440 --> 00:37:32,040
You'll learn plenty.

954
00:37:32,040 --> 00:37:33,200
That's so true.

955
00:37:33,200 --> 00:37:34,920
Whenever I wanna learn something...

956
00:37:34,950 --> 00:37:35,530
No.

957
00:37:35,530 --> 00:37:37,130
I'll just talk to Hu.

958
00:37:38,600 --> 00:37:40,120
Are you mocking me?

959
00:37:40,200 --> 00:37:41,400
No.

960
00:37:41,400 --> 00:37:43,020
Aren't you an entomologist?

961
00:37:44,920 --> 00:37:46,200
I'm a chokehold expert.

962
00:37:46,200 --> 00:37:47,360
Keep mocking me

963
00:37:47,360 --> 00:37:48,630
and I'll put you in a chokehold.

964
00:37:49,640 --> 00:37:51,880
(Curious about chokeholds)
How's a chokehold different from an armbar?

965
00:37:51,880 --> 00:37:54,400
A chokehold targets
the airway and blood vessels.

966
00:37:54,400 --> 00:37:56,600
An armbar targets the joints.

967
00:37:57,960 --> 00:37:59,360
A wrestling expert.

968
00:37:59,440 --> 00:38:01,680
Now we're talking wrestling.

969
00:38:02,360 --> 00:38:04,720
Churan, what are you good at?

970
00:38:04,720 --> 00:38:06,920
I don't know anything about this stuff.

971
00:38:06,920 --> 00:38:09,720
What do you like learning about?

972
00:38:09,800 --> 00:38:12,140
♪I've studied so many promises♪

973
00:38:12,140 --> 00:38:13,340
(Bluetooth connected)

974
00:38:13,360 --> 00:38:15,390
♪Vows of eternal love♪

975
00:38:17,000 --> 00:38:21,400
♪Because of love♪

976
00:38:24,100 --> 00:38:30,500
(Now playing:
Invisible Man by Bai Jingting)

977
00:38:30,520 --> 00:38:31,120
I get it.

978
00:38:34,820 --> 00:38:36,260
(Now playing:
One Little Drink by Jia Bing)

979
00:38:36,280 --> 00:38:36,930
Bing!

980
00:38:40,880 --> 00:38:42,720
Bing's made quite a few songs.

981
00:38:42,720 --> 00:38:43,960
When did I make these?

982
00:38:43,960 --> 00:38:44,970
I don't even remember.

983
00:38:47,320 --> 00:38:47,720
Right.

984
00:38:48,280 --> 00:38:49,420
♪Who cares?♪

985
00:38:51,280 --> 00:38:51,880
♪One drink♪

986
00:38:51,880 --> 00:38:53,360
♪A little drink or two♪

987
00:38:53,360 --> 00:38:54,520
♪One by one♪

988
00:38:54,600 --> 00:38:55,930
You picked that up fast.

989
00:38:56,720 --> 00:38:58,240
This should actually

990
00:38:58,240 --> 00:39:00,830
be classified as rap, you know?

991
00:39:01,360 --> 00:39:03,050
It's really catchy.

992
00:39:04,640 --> 00:39:05,120
Seriously though,

993
00:39:05,120 --> 00:39:06,200
I'm really looking forward

994
00:39:06,200 --> 00:39:07,440
to Bing's dinner tonight.

995
00:39:07,440 --> 00:39:09,200
I've decided to cook a few dishes too.

996
00:39:09,200 --> 00:39:10,900
Why would you wanna ruin

997
00:39:11,920 --> 00:39:13,320
a perfectly good meal?

998
00:39:14,360 --> 00:39:15,980
I'm actually pretty good at cooking now.

999
00:39:16,240 --> 00:39:18,780
I think you've
got potential, Chengcheng.

1000
00:39:19,440 --> 00:39:20,510
Bai's pretty good too.

1001
00:39:21,560 --> 00:39:22,040
You know what?

1002
00:39:22,040 --> 00:39:23,720
Know who's the worst cook?

1003
00:39:24,640 --> 00:39:25,190
Who?

1004
00:39:25,840 --> 00:39:26,820
Hu!

1005
00:39:29,200 --> 00:39:31,200
He puts eggs in
before the oil's even hot.

1006
00:39:31,200 --> 00:39:32,200
Can you believe that?

1007
00:39:32,280 --> 00:39:34,640
Hu!

1008
00:39:35,640 --> 00:39:36,570
A mosquito

1009
00:39:37,200 --> 00:39:38,680
bit my ear.

1010
00:39:38,680 --> 00:39:40,690
Now my whole ear's swollen.

1011
00:39:41,680 --> 00:39:42,400
Can you tell?

1012
00:39:42,400 --> 00:39:43,400
Not really.

1013
00:39:43,480 --> 00:39:45,240
I can't see your other ear,

1014
00:39:45,240 --> 00:39:46,340
so I can't compare.

1015
00:39:47,260 --> 00:39:48,980
(Take a look from the front)

1016
00:39:49,840 --> 00:39:51,170
Big-Eared Tutu!

1017
00:39:54,200 --> 00:39:56,080
Know Tutu's last name?

1018
00:39:56,160 --> 00:39:56,950
Chen?

1019
00:39:58,240 --> 00:39:59,200
Chen Tutu?

1020
00:40:00,720 --> 00:40:01,560
You guys didn't know?

1021
00:40:01,560 --> 00:40:02,640
Chen Tutu?

1022
00:40:02,720 --> 00:40:03,720
Hu!

1023
00:40:03,800 --> 00:40:04,670
Hu Tutu?

1024
00:40:05,370 --> 00:40:06,880
You said

1025
00:40:06,960 --> 00:40:09,680
Chen?

1026
00:40:09,680 --> 00:40:11,200
Wait, isn't it Chen Tutu?

1027
00:40:11,200 --> 00:40:11,760
Hu Tutu.

1028
00:40:11,760 --> 00:40:12,600
It's Hu Tutu.

1029
00:40:12,600 --> 00:40:13,760
Right, Hu Tutu.

1030
00:40:14,840 --> 00:40:15,680
We're here.

1031
00:40:15,680 --> 00:40:16,240
Let's go.

1032
00:40:20,520 --> 00:40:21,920
Food! Let's eat!

1033
00:40:22,080 --> 00:40:23,040
I gotta hurry

1034
00:40:23,120 --> 00:40:24,000
and get that meat stewing.

1035
00:40:24,200 --> 00:40:24,900
I'll wash it.

1036
00:40:24,900 --> 00:40:26,580
(Looking everywhere for something to do)

1037
00:40:26,600 --> 00:40:27,080
I'll wash it.

1038
00:40:27,080 --> 00:40:27,480
No need.

1039
00:40:27,480 --> 00:40:27,800
I'll do it.

1040
00:40:28,260 --> 00:40:29,420
(Nothing to do, busy working)

1041
00:40:29,440 --> 00:40:31,400
If I just sit around all day,

1042
00:40:31,400 --> 00:40:32,830
I'll end up completely useless!

1043
00:40:34,120 --> 00:40:35,560
I'll get the chicken feet going first.

1044
00:40:35,580 --> 00:40:37,020
(Bing's new dish: Chicken feet
with pig ears and soybeans)

1045
00:40:37,740 --> 00:40:39,260
(Add chicken feet to a hot, oiled pan)

1046
00:40:39,300 --> 00:40:40,460
(Add ginger, scallions,
and onions. Stir-fry)

1047
00:40:40,500 --> 00:40:41,460
(Add sliced pig ears and cilantro roots)

1048
00:40:41,500 --> 00:40:42,900
(Season with cooking wine,
vinegar, and dark soy sauce)

1049
00:40:42,940 --> 00:40:44,380
(Add soaked soybeans
and enough water to cover)

1050
00:40:44,420 --> 00:40:46,860
(Add bouillon, chili bean paste,
pepper, sugar, and cumin. Stir)

1051
00:40:46,900 --> 00:40:48,340
(Transfer to a clay pot
and simmer for 40 minutes)

1052
00:40:49,940 --> 00:40:51,300
(Meanwhile, making braised beef,
another new dish by Bing)

1053
00:40:51,340 --> 00:40:52,540
(Add beef to a hot, oiled pan)

1054
00:40:53,700 --> 00:40:54,980
(Add ginger, wine, dark soy sauce,
and vinegar. Stir-fry)

1055
00:40:55,020 --> 00:40:56,460
(Add enough hot water to cover the beef)

1056
00:40:56,810 --> 00:40:57,880
(Add salt, chili bean paste, pepper,
star anise, scallions, and onions)

1057
00:40:59,220 --> 00:41:00,580
(Transfer to a pressure cooker
for 30 minutes)

1058
00:41:00,660 --> 00:41:02,740
(Waiting for the delicious results)

1059
00:41:02,760 --> 00:41:03,960
Save me a burner!

1060
00:41:03,960 --> 00:41:05,180
(Chef Fan enters)
I'm using the big stove today!

1061
00:41:07,280 --> 00:41:07,600
Anyu,

1062
00:41:07,600 --> 00:41:08,100
wanna

1063
00:41:08,520 --> 00:41:09,320
help me?

1064
00:41:09,320 --> 00:41:10,160
I'll help.

1065
00:41:10,160 --> 00:41:10,680
Great.

1066
00:41:11,320 --> 00:41:12,380
Fry eight eggs for me.

1067
00:41:15,200 --> 00:41:16,120
Seriously?

1068
00:41:16,320 --> 00:41:17,960
I'm really good at frying eggs.

1069
00:41:17,960 --> 00:41:18,560
(Expertise +1)
You just fry them.

1070
00:41:18,560 --> 00:41:19,360
That's all there is to it.

1071
00:41:19,360 --> 00:41:20,600
Can I count on you for this?

1072
00:41:20,600 --> 00:41:21,340
No problem!

1073
00:41:21,380 --> 00:41:23,380
(Fired up again)

1074
00:41:23,400 --> 00:41:24,160
What are you making?

1075
00:41:24,160 --> 00:41:25,060
Gongjin eggs.

1076
00:41:27,620 --> 00:41:29,620
(Chef Wang and Chef Fan
team up for Gongjin eggs)

1077
00:41:29,800 --> 00:41:31,360
A dish for young people.

1078
00:41:31,440 --> 00:41:32,480
What?

1079
00:41:32,480 --> 00:41:33,040
What kind of eggs?

1080
00:41:33,040 --> 00:41:34,200
Gongjin eggs.

1081
00:41:34,200 --> 00:41:34,880
What's that?

1082
00:41:35,580 --> 00:41:37,060
(This is it)

1083
00:41:37,400 --> 00:41:38,100
Oh my God.

1084
00:41:42,800 --> 00:41:43,560
Success!

1085
00:41:43,560 --> 00:41:45,440
What's that black stuff around it?

1086
00:41:45,520 --> 00:41:46,440
Those are scallions.

1087
00:41:46,440 --> 00:41:47,600
(Mystery solved)
Scallions.

1088
00:41:47,600 --> 00:41:48,250
Let's make the sauce.

1089
00:41:48,620 --> 00:41:50,460
(Preparing the sauce
for Gongjin eggs)

1090
00:41:50,500 --> 00:41:52,140
(Two chefs join forces
to make the sauce)

1091
00:41:52,480 --> 00:41:53,160
Okay, that's enough.

1092
00:41:53,160 --> 00:41:54,980
Just pour the sauce in.

1093
00:41:56,740 --> 00:41:58,100
(Studying carefully)

1094
00:41:58,120 --> 00:41:58,980
Let's plate it.

1095
00:42:01,560 --> 00:42:02,480
That smell

1096
00:42:02,480 --> 00:42:03,910
is pretty promising.

1097
00:42:04,480 --> 00:42:05,600
It's way more

1098
00:42:05,600 --> 00:42:06,700
than just promising!

1099
00:42:10,500 --> 00:42:13,060
(Can't wait)

1100
00:42:13,340 --> 00:42:15,340
(Absolutely amazing)

1101
00:42:15,640 --> 00:42:15,880
Nice.

1102
00:42:15,880 --> 00:42:16,360
Is it good?

1103
00:42:16,360 --> 00:42:16,940
Delicious.

1104
00:42:17,820 --> 00:42:19,500
(Food critic mode activated)

1105
00:42:20,920 --> 00:42:21,780
It's not bad.

1106
00:42:22,460 --> 00:42:23,900
(What kind of compliment is that?)

1107
00:42:24,200 --> 00:42:24,960
Churan, try some!

1108
00:42:24,960 --> 00:42:26,430
Your dish is my competition.

1109
00:42:27,320 --> 00:42:28,320
You mean the eggs?

1110
00:42:28,320 --> 00:42:28,760
Yeah.

1111
00:42:29,100 --> 00:42:30,780
(Another egg dish
enters the competition)

1112
00:42:30,840 --> 00:42:32,040
Tomato and egg stir-fry?

1113
00:42:32,120 --> 00:42:32,580
Yeah.

1114
00:42:32,620 --> 00:42:33,940
(A new challenger?)

1115
00:42:34,140 --> 00:42:35,860
(Set the cooked eggs aside)

1116
00:42:37,740 --> 00:42:38,820
(Extra careful)

1117
00:42:43,820 --> 00:42:46,220
(Like a majestic waterfall)

1118
00:42:52,080 --> 00:42:52,750
I'm telling you.

1119
00:42:53,360 --> 00:42:53,970
It's definitely

1120
00:42:54,520 --> 00:42:55,780
(Watching closely)
looking amazing now.

1121
00:42:59,060 --> 00:43:00,340
(Satisfied)

1122
00:43:09,160 --> 00:43:09,920
What's wrong?

1123
00:43:10,440 --> 00:43:10,900
It's black.

1124
00:43:11,480 --> 00:43:12,260
What's black?

1125
00:43:12,820 --> 00:43:13,270
Why...

1126
00:43:14,480 --> 00:43:15,640
What's turned black?

1127
00:43:15,720 --> 00:43:16,510
The eggs!

1128
00:43:18,400 --> 00:43:19,150
They're burnt.

1129
00:43:19,300 --> 00:43:20,980
(Nearly had a heart attack)

1130
00:43:21,000 --> 00:43:21,280
It's fine.

1131
00:43:21,280 --> 00:43:21,880
Should still be okay.

1132
00:43:21,880 --> 00:43:22,590
It should taste good.

1133
00:43:25,800 --> 00:43:26,440
Try some.

1134
00:43:26,440 --> 00:43:27,400
(Offering a taste)
It should be good.

1135
00:43:27,400 --> 00:43:28,040
(Thanks, but no thanks)
It's delicious.

1136
00:43:28,040 --> 00:43:29,040
It really is good.

1137
00:43:29,040 --> 00:43:30,280
I don't like chocolate.

1138
00:43:33,620 --> 00:43:35,900
(Trying to cover it up)

1139
00:43:36,280 --> 00:43:37,800
Let it cool first.

1140
00:43:37,880 --> 00:43:40,220
(Airing it out)
Let that burnt smell fade.

1141
00:43:40,840 --> 00:43:41,760
All done.

1142
00:43:41,840 --> 00:43:42,740
Why's everyone cooking eggs?

1143
00:43:42,740 --> 00:43:43,680
(Tomato eggs,
Gongjin eggs, yellow chive eggs)

1144
00:43:43,680 --> 00:43:44,200
Well,

1145
00:43:44,200 --> 00:43:45,460
I'm definitely winning.

1146
00:43:46,200 --> 00:43:47,120
(Back from training)
Tomato and egg stir-fry?

1147
00:43:47,120 --> 00:43:47,620
Yeah.

1148
00:43:48,460 --> 00:43:49,620
(Yellow chive eggs, taught by Bing)

1149
00:43:49,640 --> 00:43:52,200
Get the pan smoking hot.

1150
00:43:52,220 --> 00:43:53,160
(Secret cooking technique)
That's how you make it delicious.

1151
00:43:54,340 --> 00:43:55,940
(Starting to smoke)

1152
00:43:55,960 --> 00:43:56,440
Can I add them now?

1153
00:43:56,440 --> 00:43:57,030
Go ahead.

1154
00:43:57,960 --> 00:43:59,280
Yes! We need that sizzle!

1155
00:43:59,280 --> 00:44:00,880
Don't touch it yet.

1156
00:44:00,880 --> 00:44:01,720
(Let the eggs set before stirring)

1157
00:44:01,720 --> 00:44:02,300
Stir it.

1158
00:44:03,760 --> 00:44:04,700
Add some soy sauce.

1159
00:44:04,700 --> 00:44:05,660
(Add soy sauce, oyster sauce, and MSG)

1160
00:44:06,140 --> 00:44:07,240
(Add yellow chives and stir-fry)
Keep stirring.

1161
00:44:07,240 --> 00:44:08,040
Now it's ready to serve.

1162
00:44:10,880 --> 00:44:11,640
All done.

1163
00:44:11,720 --> 00:44:12,240
Beautiful.

1164
00:44:15,320 --> 00:44:16,150
Bing approves.

1165
00:44:16,420 --> 00:44:18,060
(Bing's seal of approval: Delicious)

1166
00:44:18,340 --> 00:44:19,260
(A giant hand appears)

1167
00:44:19,420 --> 00:44:21,700
(The food critic returns)

1168
00:44:25,720 --> 00:44:26,800
Is it hot or good?

1169
00:44:27,000 --> 00:44:27,730
It's too hot!

1170
00:44:28,420 --> 00:44:29,500
(Why'd I even ask?)

1171
00:44:30,080 --> 00:44:31,440
It's not bad.

1172
00:44:31,440 --> 00:44:32,620
What do you mean, "not bad"?

1173
00:44:33,680 --> 00:44:34,320
It's okay.

1174
00:44:34,400 --> 00:44:36,520
(So hard to give credit?)
You just won't admit it's good!

1175
00:44:36,600 --> 00:44:37,960
(Cooking rookies)
Those two are still beginners.

1176
00:44:37,960 --> 00:44:38,940
(The real Bai)
I'm the senior here.

1177
00:44:38,940 --> 00:44:39,580
(Already on another level)

1178
00:44:40,620 --> 00:44:42,980
(The three-way egg showdown ends)

1179
00:44:43,720 --> 00:44:45,080
Do we have bullfrogs? Probably not.

1180
00:44:47,040 --> 00:44:48,040
Even the side dishes...

1181
00:44:48,040 --> 00:44:49,720
He only asks because we don't have any!

1182
00:44:50,800 --> 00:44:51,940
That's why I can challenge myself.

1183
00:44:53,060 --> 00:44:55,220
(Suddenly looking around)

1184
00:44:59,800 --> 00:45:00,480
What else do we have?

1185
00:45:00,500 --> 00:45:01,760
(The senior chef shows off again)
Chicken wings.

1186
00:45:01,760 --> 00:45:02,580
What's this?

1187
00:45:04,040 --> 00:45:05,200
Pork ribs.

1188
00:45:05,280 --> 00:45:06,100
Black bean pork ribs.

1189
00:45:06,100 --> 00:45:07,500
(Chef Fan's new dish:
Black bean pork ribs)

1190
00:45:07,580 --> 00:45:09,260
(Measuring precisely)

1191
00:45:11,920 --> 00:45:12,490
What's that?

1192
00:45:13,120 --> 00:45:13,890
Black bean pork ribs.

1193
00:45:14,180 --> 00:45:16,060
(Still cooking?)

1194
00:45:21,040 --> 00:45:22,500
Where should I put this?

1195
00:45:23,060 --> 00:45:25,060
(Let me help you)

1196
00:45:25,720 --> 00:45:26,760
No, it's too hot.

1197
00:45:26,760 --> 00:45:27,360
Here, hold this.

1198
00:45:27,360 --> 00:45:28,120
I'll do it for you.

1199
00:45:28,120 --> 00:45:28,740
Thanks, Hu.

1200
00:45:30,180 --> 00:45:31,620
(Such a sweet talker)

1201
00:45:31,960 --> 00:45:33,570
That sent shivers down my spine!

1202
00:45:34,840 --> 00:45:35,900
Easy. Don't burn yourself.

1203
00:45:35,900 --> 00:45:37,780
(Shaken, but secretly loving it)

1204
00:45:39,020 --> 00:45:40,900
(Steaming the black bean pork ribs)
Steam for 20 minutes.

1205
00:45:41,460 --> 00:45:43,260
(Black bean pork ribs)

1206
00:45:45,040 --> 00:45:46,620
Maybe I'll make some chicken wings.

1207
00:45:46,620 --> 00:45:47,540
(Secretly getting competitive)

1208
00:45:48,120 --> 00:45:49,010
What are you making?

1209
00:45:49,360 --> 00:45:51,360
I checked out this chicken wing recipe.

1210
00:45:51,360 --> 00:45:52,480
You gotta marinate them first,

1211
00:45:52,480 --> 00:45:53,980
then wait 20 minutes.

1212
00:45:54,880 --> 00:45:56,530
Chicken wings aren't easy.

1213
00:45:56,840 --> 00:45:57,700
Perfect for me.

1214
00:45:57,700 --> 00:45:59,140
(The harder, the better)

1215
00:45:59,160 --> 00:46:00,780
You love a challenge.

1216
00:46:00,780 --> 00:46:02,520
(Scoring wings for flavor)
Make a few cuts.

1217
00:46:02,600 --> 00:46:03,440
What's that?

1218
00:46:03,440 --> 00:46:04,920
(Marinate with sauces and salt for 20 mins)
Chicken wings.

1219
00:46:05,000 --> 00:46:05,730
Candied ones?

1220
00:46:06,920 --> 00:46:09,080
(Keyword spotted)
Don't ask Bing about candied wings.

1221
00:46:09,080 --> 00:46:10,180
(The inventor of candied chicken wings)
Your master is right here.

1222
00:46:10,380 --> 00:46:11,740
(No lessons needed)

1223
00:46:11,860 --> 00:46:13,740
(Fry the marinated wings
until golden brown)

1224
00:46:14,120 --> 00:46:15,260
Fried chicken wings?

1225
00:46:16,400 --> 00:46:16,840
Try some.

1226
00:46:16,840 --> 00:46:17,950
Tomato and egg stir-fry.

1227
00:46:18,140 --> 00:46:19,860
(Right now?)

1228
00:46:20,360 --> 00:46:21,200
That's been sitting there

1229
00:46:21,200 --> 00:46:22,160
for almost an hour!

1230
00:46:22,160 --> 00:46:22,640
And now you want me to try it?

1231
00:46:22,640 --> 00:46:23,280
No!

1232
00:46:23,280 --> 00:46:25,070
Now's the perfect time to taste it!

1233
00:46:25,380 --> 00:46:26,540
(Who can resist
the perfect tasting time?)

1234
00:46:27,240 --> 00:46:28,040
You gotta eat the eggs

1235
00:46:28,040 --> 00:46:29,220
with the tomatoes.

1236
00:46:33,220 --> 00:46:34,580
(Full of anticipation)
Isn't it amazing?

1237
00:46:35,040 --> 00:46:35,630
Amazing.

1238
00:46:36,960 --> 00:46:38,050
Seriously amazing.

1239
00:46:38,280 --> 00:46:39,440
It's really good, right?

1240
00:46:39,440 --> 00:46:40,760
Compared to those

1241
00:46:40,760 --> 00:46:42,370
burnt chicken wings of yours...

1242
00:46:42,560 --> 00:46:44,120
My chicken wings!

1243
00:46:44,520 --> 00:46:45,770
You're still making burnt wings?

1244
00:46:46,020 --> 00:46:47,340
(What's that supposed to mean?)

1245
00:46:47,360 --> 00:46:47,720
You know what?

1246
00:46:47,720 --> 00:46:48,760
That outfit of yours

1247
00:46:48,760 --> 00:46:50,740
makes you look like a real chef.

1248
00:46:50,740 --> 00:46:51,620
(Looking the part)

1249
00:46:51,640 --> 00:46:53,000
With that little black towel,

1250
00:46:53,000 --> 00:46:55,340
you look like you're
on Culinary Class Wars!

1251
00:46:55,340 --> 00:46:56,700
(Black-clad Chef Bai)

1252
00:46:56,820 --> 00:46:57,780
(Time to stir-fry!)

1253
00:46:58,340 --> 00:47:01,140
(The master chef has arrived!)

1254
00:47:06,380 --> 00:47:07,700
(Oh!)

1255
00:47:07,700 --> 00:47:09,460
(One more time)

1256
00:47:10,280 --> 00:47:10,820
Looks good.

1257
00:47:10,940 --> 00:47:11,620
(Bing approves once again)

1258
00:47:11,640 --> 00:47:12,260
Into the bowl!

1259
00:47:12,980 --> 00:47:15,500
(Another masterpiece by Chef Bai:
Dry-fried chicken wings)

1260
00:47:15,520 --> 00:47:16,240
I'll make something too.

1261
00:47:16,240 --> 00:47:17,800
(Stop trying to compete!)
Don't, Hu.

1262
00:47:17,880 --> 00:47:18,920
We were just talking in the car.

1263
00:47:18,920 --> 00:47:20,400
We all agreed

1264
00:47:20,400 --> 00:47:21,720
you're the worst cook.

1265
00:47:21,800 --> 00:47:22,520
Seriously?

1266
00:47:22,520 --> 00:47:23,200
He said it.

1267
00:47:23,200 --> 00:47:24,680
(Can't keep a secret, huh?)
Teng, why'd you do me like that?

1268
00:47:24,920 --> 00:47:26,260
That's how I roast you.

1269
00:47:28,240 --> 00:47:30,560
(Time to consult the online expert)
I can fry some potatoes.

1270
00:47:30,640 --> 00:47:33,020
I can't possibly mess up frying, right?

1271
00:47:33,600 --> 00:47:34,680
Go ahead if you want to.

1272
00:47:35,100 --> 00:47:36,740
(His comeback dish: Crispy potatoes)

1273
00:47:36,760 --> 00:47:38,420
Know how to cut rolling chunks?

1274
00:47:40,300 --> 00:47:42,180
(Doing it himself)

1275
00:47:42,260 --> 00:47:43,140
(Steam the potato chunks for 25 minutes)

1276
00:47:43,160 --> 00:47:43,600
Okay.

1277
00:47:43,600 --> 00:47:44,410
Time to fry!

1278
00:47:44,660 --> 00:47:46,860
(I'm taking back what's mine)

1279
00:47:46,880 --> 00:47:49,040
Add the potatoes when the oil's hot.

1280
00:47:49,120 --> 00:47:50,550
Five minutes on low heat.

1281
00:47:53,640 --> 00:47:54,480
Now we're getting somewhere.

1282
00:47:55,120 --> 00:47:56,460
I can smell the potatoes.

1283
00:47:57,200 --> 00:47:57,800
Almost done, right?

1284
00:47:57,800 --> 00:47:58,920
Feels like

1285
00:47:58,920 --> 00:48:00,120
they're about

1286
00:48:00,120 --> 00:48:00,980
to burn.

1287
00:48:01,020 --> 00:48:02,620
(Can't let them burn!)

1288
00:48:05,220 --> 00:48:06,980
(Making his own seasoning)

1289
00:48:12,620 --> 00:48:15,140
(Taste test)

1290
00:48:15,480 --> 00:48:16,160
Delicious.

1291
00:48:16,360 --> 00:48:17,360
Please try some.

1292
00:48:17,360 --> 00:48:18,380
Smells pretty good.

1293
00:48:19,520 --> 00:48:19,800
Good?

1294
00:48:19,800 --> 00:48:20,200
Not bad.

1295
00:48:22,100 --> 00:48:23,300
(Waiting anxiously)

1296
00:48:23,370 --> 00:48:23,910
Delicious.

1297
00:48:24,880 --> 00:48:26,240
These potatoes look really unhealthy.

1298
00:48:28,160 --> 00:48:29,600
Hu's sweating buckets!

1299
00:48:29,600 --> 00:48:31,340
(Still determined)
Hold this and cool off!

1300
00:48:32,960 --> 00:48:35,560
Frying these is way too hot!

1301
00:48:35,640 --> 00:48:36,350
Delicious!

1302
00:48:37,020 --> 00:48:39,980
(I'm not the worst cook anymore!
Crispy potatoes)

1303
00:48:40,000 --> 00:48:40,920
What's this, Bing?

1304
00:48:40,920 --> 00:48:43,020
Soybean paste stew.

1305
00:48:43,140 --> 00:48:43,980
(Soybean paste stew)

1306
00:48:43,980 --> 00:48:45,340
(Add onions, zucchini, bean sprouts,
enoki mushrooms, pork, and chilies)

1307
00:48:45,820 --> 00:48:47,500
(Fill with boiling water)

1308
00:48:47,540 --> 00:48:48,740
(Add chili sauce, Korean bibimbap sauce,
and barbecue seasoning. Mix well)

1309
00:48:48,780 --> 00:48:49,540
(Crack in an egg.
Add green peppers and scallions)

1310
00:48:50,240 --> 00:48:51,280
That smells amazing, Bing!

1311
00:48:51,280 --> 00:48:52,760
I can smell it from way over here!

1312
00:48:52,760 --> 00:48:54,020
Try it while it's hot.
Check the seasoning.

1313
00:48:57,480 --> 00:48:58,400
Amazing!

1314
00:48:58,480 --> 00:48:59,520
It's so savory!

1315
00:48:59,520 --> 00:49:00,720
Perfectly seasoned.

1316
00:49:00,720 --> 00:49:01,440
Before serving,

1317
00:49:01,440 --> 00:49:03,200
add some Totole reduced-sodium
chicken seasoning.

1318
00:49:03,200 --> 00:49:05,200
It's made with real chicken,

1319
00:49:05,200 --> 00:49:05,920
scallions, and garlic.

1320
00:49:05,920 --> 00:49:07,720
25% less salt, even more flavor!

1321
00:49:07,720 --> 00:49:09,640
That flavor really comes alive!

1322
00:49:12,360 --> 00:49:14,320
I'll get the cold noodle broth ready.

1323
00:49:14,400 --> 00:49:15,620
(Upgraded cold noodles)
It's been upgraded.

1324
00:49:15,960 --> 00:49:17,360
This broth has so much stuff!

1325
00:49:17,360 --> 00:49:18,840
(What are you saying?)
I mean, so many ingredients!

1326
00:49:18,840 --> 00:49:19,600
Cold noodle broth?

1327
00:49:19,600 --> 00:49:20,480
I know.

1328
00:49:20,480 --> 00:49:21,400
There's so much in it!

1329
00:49:24,260 --> 00:49:26,850
(Still cooking: Cold noodles,
braised beef, and black bean pork ribs)

1330
00:49:26,880 --> 00:49:27,560
Got any board games?

1331
00:49:27,560 --> 00:49:28,360
Chinese chess?

1332
00:49:28,360 --> 00:49:29,520
(Eager to show off his skills)
My specialty.

1333
00:49:29,520 --> 00:49:30,480
(Skills: Calling cops, chess with Teng)
Playing chess with Teng.

1334
00:49:30,480 --> 00:49:31,610
Gomoku works too.

1335
00:49:32,760 --> 00:49:35,080
I'm actually pretty good at Gomoku.

1336
00:49:35,080 --> 00:49:35,660
Really?

1337
00:49:35,660 --> 00:49:36,460
(Confident)

1338
00:49:36,680 --> 00:49:37,710
Let's play chess then.

1339
00:49:40,360 --> 00:49:41,040
Watching the game.

1340
00:49:41,060 --> 00:49:42,180
(Hands behind his back)

1341
00:49:42,400 --> 00:49:42,870
After you.

1342
00:49:43,820 --> 00:49:45,380
(Black pieces, White pieces)

1343
00:49:45,700 --> 00:49:46,190
Go ahead.

1344
00:49:48,460 --> 00:49:49,940
(No taking back moves)

1345
00:49:54,600 --> 00:49:56,050
He's just mirroring every move.

1346
00:50:11,350 --> 00:50:13,040
The winning move is here!

1347
00:50:15,300 --> 00:50:16,660
(The winner is decided)

1348
00:50:20,540 --> 00:50:21,260
(Give it a shake)

1349
00:50:21,500 --> 00:50:22,580
(Some impressive skills)

1350
00:50:22,880 --> 00:50:24,840
Flip the board

1351
00:50:24,920 --> 00:50:26,680
and stormed off!

1352
00:50:26,680 --> 00:50:28,340
After just eight moves!

1353
00:50:28,740 --> 00:50:30,020
(Only eight moves)

1354
00:50:30,040 --> 00:50:31,520
What a short match!

1355
00:50:31,680 --> 00:50:32,840
Eight moves?

1356
00:50:32,840 --> 00:50:34,270
Demi-Gods and Eight Moves?

1357
00:50:34,800 --> 00:50:36,560
Remember when I said

1358
00:50:36,560 --> 00:50:37,930
I was good at this? Cut that out!

1359
00:50:39,720 --> 00:50:40,460
Here, you go first.

1360
00:50:40,700 --> 00:50:42,820
(Huang Jingyu: black, Shen Teng: white)

1361
00:50:43,200 --> 00:50:44,240
Triangle formation.

1362
00:50:44,320 --> 00:50:44,820
No.

1363
00:50:45,880 --> 00:50:46,800
Amateur formation.

1364
00:50:52,080 --> 00:50:53,000
Square formation!

1365
00:50:53,000 --> 00:50:54,640
Go!

1366
00:50:56,240 --> 00:50:56,800
Capture it!

1367
00:50:56,800 --> 00:50:58,680
That's called Go, right?

1368
00:50:58,840 --> 00:50:59,380
Let me see.

1369
00:50:59,380 --> 00:51:00,500
(Right up his alley)

1370
00:51:00,800 --> 00:51:03,680
I'm just one move away!

1371
00:51:03,680 --> 00:51:04,760
Teng,

1372
00:51:04,760 --> 00:51:06,380
just one move!

1373
00:51:06,920 --> 00:51:08,260
The winning move is coming!

1374
00:51:08,740 --> 00:51:10,060
(Double open three. One move away)

1375
00:51:10,080 --> 00:51:10,920
But

1376
00:51:10,920 --> 00:51:12,780
(Feeling smug)
you haven't spotted it!

1377
00:51:13,520 --> 00:51:14,240
You've only got

1378
00:51:16,040 --> 00:51:16,850
one chance.

1379
00:51:19,680 --> 00:51:20,380
Teng spotted it.

1380
00:51:20,380 --> 00:51:21,540
(Completely blocked)

1381
00:51:27,280 --> 00:51:28,320
Where?

1382
00:51:28,320 --> 00:51:30,260
He blocked my double open three!

1383
00:51:30,820 --> 00:51:32,300
(So close, yet so far)

1384
00:51:34,880 --> 00:51:35,920
Then aren't you

1385
00:51:35,920 --> 00:51:36,850
done for?

1386
00:51:38,940 --> 00:51:41,060
(Double open three completed)

1387
00:51:44,200 --> 00:51:44,790
You're done.

1388
00:51:45,340 --> 00:51:46,780
(Trying to salvage it)

1389
00:51:46,820 --> 00:51:47,940
(A double-handed defense)

1390
00:51:51,400 --> 00:51:52,370
It's already over.

1391
00:51:54,940 --> 00:51:56,680
(Churan: Black, Teng: White)
Let's play winner stays on.

1392
00:51:56,680 --> 00:51:57,490
Loser steps aside.

1393
00:52:04,440 --> 00:52:06,080
Fast and steady moves.

1394
00:52:08,960 --> 00:52:10,480
The winning move is coming!

1395
00:52:16,300 --> 00:52:18,020
(Looks defensive,
but it's a winning move)

1396
00:52:18,300 --> 00:52:19,340
(Didn't notice)

1397
00:52:19,360 --> 00:52:20,230
Just dragging it out.

1398
00:52:23,480 --> 00:52:24,750
I won!

1399
00:52:25,800 --> 00:52:27,510
One, two, three, four.

1400
00:52:32,000 --> 00:52:32,750
Flip it!

1401
00:52:35,080 --> 00:52:35,620
Come on!

1402
00:52:35,980 --> 00:52:37,660
(Wang Anyu: White, Wang Churan: Black)

1403
00:52:40,140 --> 00:52:41,620
(Double open three. One move away)

1404
00:52:44,280 --> 00:52:45,110
Sideways formation!

1405
00:52:46,160 --> 00:52:47,080
Zigzagging around, huh?

1406
00:52:47,080 --> 00:52:47,890
Zigzagging.

1407
00:52:48,140 --> 00:52:50,060
(Double open three in position)

1408
00:52:50,960 --> 00:52:51,760
I won.

1409
00:52:51,760 --> 00:52:52,790
One, two, three, four.

1410
00:52:53,200 --> 00:52:53,740
