1676
01:01:08,240 --> 01:01:09,610
His dish really wasn't good.

1677
01:01:11,080 --> 01:01:12,010
It gets stuck in your teeth.

1678
01:01:12,880 --> 01:01:13,680
Right?

1679
01:01:13,680 --> 01:01:16,160
Ever had fatty meat stuck in your teeth?

1680
01:01:17,320 --> 01:01:18,650
It just happened to me.

1681
01:01:19,780 --> 01:01:21,620
(Ignoring the bad reviews)

1682
01:01:21,680 --> 01:01:23,200
See if we can wash those ribs off.

1683
01:01:23,200 --> 01:01:24,320
Then see if another chef

1684
01:01:24,320 --> 01:01:24,960
can save them.

1685
01:01:25,780 --> 01:01:26,980
=Natural High S4=

1686
01:01:35,100 --> 01:01:37,980
(Carb overload)

1687
01:01:42,000 --> 01:01:43,360
Anyone got digestive tablets?

1688
01:01:43,440 --> 01:01:44,600
Give me one.

1689
01:01:44,840 --> 01:01:45,800
Time for digestive tablets?

1690
01:01:45,800 --> 01:01:47,590
I feel like the noodles
are swelling in my stomach.

1691
01:01:49,440 --> 01:01:51,440
They're not as thin
as when you ate them.

1692
01:01:51,440 --> 01:01:52,680
I feel like they've

1693
01:01:52,680 --> 01:01:54,120
gotten thicker and bigger!

1694
01:01:54,120 --> 01:01:55,560
What do you think "swells in water"

1695
01:01:55,560 --> 01:01:56,470
means?

1696
01:01:58,460 --> 01:02:00,400
Hello, everyone!

1697
01:02:00,400 --> 01:02:01,560
Dr. Chen!

1698
01:02:02,520 --> 01:02:03,160
On Earth,

1699
01:02:03,160 --> 01:02:04,840
there's a type of plant that dances.

1700
01:02:04,840 --> 01:02:05,880
When it hears music,

1701
01:02:05,880 --> 01:02:07,490
its little leaves start moving.

1702
01:02:08,480 --> 01:02:09,840
It's not the wind.

1703
01:02:09,840 --> 01:02:11,940
Its leaves really are moving.

1704
01:02:13,400 --> 01:02:15,420
It's a fascinating
biological phenomenon.

1705
01:02:15,880 --> 01:02:18,200
You can even find it here in Hainan.

1706
01:02:18,200 --> 01:02:19,240
It's called...

1707
01:02:19,320 --> 01:02:20,720
(Dancing plant)
It's called a dancing plant.

1708
01:02:20,720 --> 01:02:21,800
As in dancing.

1709
01:02:21,880 --> 01:02:23,090
Dancing plant?

1710
01:02:26,910 --> 01:02:27,960
Dancing plant.

1711
01:02:27,960 --> 01:02:29,600
Alright.

1712
01:02:29,680 --> 01:02:30,240
Actually,

1713
01:02:30,240 --> 01:02:32,040
it doesn't really understand music.

1714
01:02:32,040 --> 01:02:33,560
It responds to certain frequencies

1715
01:02:33,560 --> 01:02:34,960
of vibrations in the air.

1716
01:02:34,960 --> 01:02:37,240
It detects high-frequency vibrations,

1717
01:02:37,240 --> 01:02:40,480
like insects chewing on leaves.

1718
01:02:40,560 --> 01:02:41,400
When it hears

1719
01:02:41,400 --> 01:02:42,280
that sound nearby,

1720
01:02:42,280 --> 01:02:44,040
it starts moving its leaves

1721
01:02:44,040 --> 01:02:45,160
to make it look like

1722
01:02:45,160 --> 01:02:47,440
another insect's already on it.

1723
01:02:47,440 --> 01:02:48,440
This confuses predators

1724
01:02:48,440 --> 01:02:49,960
and keeps it safe.

1725
01:02:49,960 --> 01:02:52,320
But one of its enemies is the aphid.

1726
01:02:52,320 --> 01:02:53,360
(Dancing plant enemy: aphids)
They have piercing mouthparts.

1727
01:02:53,360 --> 01:02:54,560
It doesn't bite. It sucks.

1728
01:02:54,760 --> 01:02:55,760
Aphids can release

1729
01:02:55,760 --> 01:02:56,840
substances that paralyze
the dancing plant.

1730
01:02:56,840 --> 01:02:58,240
So today, we're doing

1731
01:02:58,240 --> 01:02:59,960
a dancing plant challenge.

1732
01:02:59,960 --> 01:03:01,560
Seven of you will
be dancing plants (good guys),

1733
01:03:01,560 --> 01:03:02,400
and one will be an aphid (wolf).

1734
01:03:02,400 --> 01:03:03,360
Each dancing plant (good guy) gets

1735
01:03:03,360 --> 01:03:04,800
one chance to open
their eyes and do a task.

1736
01:03:04,800 --> 01:03:05,480
The dancing plants (good guys)

1737
01:03:05,480 --> 01:03:06,680
must reach the center platform

1738
01:03:06,680 --> 01:03:07,640
and dance along with the video.

1739
01:03:07,640 --> 01:03:09,660
(Mark the paper after completing a task)
Then mark the paper when they're done.

1740
01:03:09,900 --> 01:03:11,320
If the dancing plants (good guys)
complete

1741
01:03:11,320 --> 01:03:12,240
three tasks, they win.

1742
01:03:12,240 --> 01:03:14,440
Tasks can be done alone or in pairs.

1743
01:03:14,440 --> 01:03:16,200
The aphid (wolf)
can open their eyes anytime.

1744
01:03:16,200 --> 01:03:17,880
(Eye-contact Werewolf)
With eye contact and shoulder taps,

1745
01:03:17,880 --> 01:03:19,000
they can eliminate
dancing plants (good guys).

1746
01:03:19,080 --> 01:03:20,240
Dancing plants (good guys) can

1747
01:03:20,240 --> 01:03:21,080
open their eyes
and raise the alarm anytime

1748
01:03:21,080 --> 01:03:21,920
to discuss what happened

1749
01:03:21,920 --> 01:03:23,120
and vote someone out.

1750
01:03:23,200 --> 01:03:24,440
(Alarm system)
If they vote out the aphid (wolf),

1751
01:03:24,440 --> 01:03:25,760
(Alarm system)
they also win.

1752
01:03:25,760 --> 01:03:27,560
The aphid (wolf) wins by stopping

1753
01:03:27,560 --> 01:03:28,760
the tasks from being completed.

1754
01:03:28,760 --> 01:03:30,160
Alright, thank you, everyone!

1755
01:03:32,200 --> 01:03:34,680
So the wolf can't destroy...

1756
01:03:34,680 --> 01:03:35,520
(No tampering)
The paper?

1757
01:03:35,520 --> 01:03:35,850
Okay.

1758
01:03:36,560 --> 01:03:37,000
Let's go.

1759
01:03:37,000 --> 01:03:37,760
(Eye-contact Werewolf)
Pick a card.

1760
01:03:37,760 --> 01:03:38,080
Yeah.

1761
01:03:38,080 --> 01:03:38,850
Let's stop overthinking it.

1762
01:03:39,860 --> 01:03:42,820
(Randomly picking role cards)

1763
01:03:44,800 --> 01:03:46,480
Let the folks in Wanning hear you!

1764
01:03:46,560 --> 01:03:47,920
Keep it real!

1765
01:03:47,920 --> 01:03:48,980
Let them hear Bai sing!

1766
01:03:57,140 --> 01:03:59,580
(Looking left)

1767
01:03:59,580 --> 01:04:01,660
(Looking right)

1768
01:04:05,640 --> 01:04:07,720
Everyone, close your eyes.

1769
01:04:07,800 --> 01:04:08,730
Aphid, open your eyes.

1770
01:04:10,140 --> 01:04:11,820
(This round's aphid)

1771
01:04:11,840 --> 01:04:12,880
Aphid, close your eyes.

1772
01:04:15,240 --> 01:04:15,690
Start!

1773
01:04:16,240 --> 01:04:16,720
Let's go!

1774
01:04:16,720 --> 01:04:17,910
I'll go with Anyu!

1775
01:04:18,420 --> 01:04:20,420
(Ready to hunt)

1776
01:04:20,460 --> 01:04:21,180
(One look and you're dead)

1777
01:04:21,200 --> 01:04:22,000
Wait. Okay!

1778
01:04:22,000 --> 01:04:22,360
Come on!

1779
01:04:22,360 --> 01:04:23,370
Let's go!

1780
01:04:23,530 --> 01:04:24,490
We're coming!

1781
01:04:26,660 --> 01:04:28,620
(Inventing a rapid-fire
hunting technique)

1782
01:04:33,940 --> 01:04:35,580
(Definitely not a scallop)

1783
01:04:35,620 --> 01:04:37,740
(Looking for the next victim)

1784
01:04:37,780 --> 01:04:39,020
(Bai Jingting out)

1785
01:04:39,580 --> 01:04:41,860
(Cluelessly completing the task)

1786
01:04:46,060 --> 01:04:47,700
(Danger behind him)

1787
01:04:54,220 --> 01:04:55,780
(Wang Anyu out)

1788
01:05:00,780 --> 01:05:04,950
Alarm!

1789
01:05:05,300 --> 01:05:06,900
(Shaking with laughter)

1790
01:05:08,240 --> 01:05:08,660
What happened?

1791
01:05:10,000 --> 01:05:10,640
This old guy

1792
01:05:11,280 --> 01:05:13,320
kept swinging his knife at me!

1793
01:05:13,400 --> 01:05:15,480
Anyone who sees me better run.

1794
01:05:15,480 --> 01:05:16,580
That's just how I am.

1795
01:05:16,900 --> 01:05:17,780
(Achievement unlocked:
Xu Fu's Phantom Blade)

1796
01:05:17,880 --> 01:05:19,850
He's gone completely wild!

1797
01:05:23,000 --> 01:05:24,800
You've got some talent for rapping.

1798
01:05:24,800 --> 01:05:26,240
I wanna be a superhero!

1799
01:05:26,240 --> 01:05:27,120
Keep it real!

1800
01:05:27,200 --> 01:05:28,880
I thought Teng was waving at me.

1801
01:05:28,880 --> 01:05:29,760
So I opened my eyes

1802
01:05:29,760 --> 01:05:31,080
and tried to see who it was.

1803
01:05:31,080 --> 01:05:31,720
Then I saw him!

1804
01:05:34,120 --> 01:05:36,480
I didn't know he was Medusa.

1805
01:05:36,480 --> 01:05:37,360
You know?

1806
01:05:37,360 --> 01:05:39,000
One look and you're dead!

1807
01:05:40,460 --> 01:05:41,020
(This round's aphid loses)

1808
01:05:41,040 --> 01:05:42,640
How'd it end so fast?

1809
01:05:42,640 --> 01:05:44,240
I used to get eliminated
in round one too,

1810
01:05:44,240 --> 01:05:45,940
but I was always falsely accused.

1811
01:05:47,680 --> 01:05:48,900
The fastest game of Werewolf ever!

1812
01:05:48,900 --> 01:05:51,010
(New record: fastest wolf
caught in Natural High history)

1813
01:05:51,040 --> 01:05:51,970
Come on. Let's go again.

1814
01:05:52,380 --> 01:05:55,460
(Eye-contact Werewolf:
round two begins)

1815
01:05:55,760 --> 01:05:57,540
Let's see if you survive round two.

1816
01:05:58,480 --> 01:06:00,760
I think we should play standing up.

1817
01:06:00,840 --> 01:06:02,000
Makes sense.

1818
01:06:02,080 --> 01:06:02,590
Good point.

1819
01:06:02,700 --> 01:06:04,540
(Keeping outside distractions
to a minimum)

1820
01:06:05,480 --> 01:06:06,960
Can we play Bai's part of the song?

1821
01:06:06,960 --> 01:06:08,690
We didn't even get to his part!

1822
01:06:08,700 --> 01:06:10,580
(Even Keep it real
can't get past round two)

1823
01:06:19,900 --> 01:06:20,820
(A bird's-eye view)

1824
01:06:20,840 --> 01:06:21,720
I'm calling the alarm

1825
01:06:21,720 --> 01:06:22,690
if you keep this up!

1826
01:06:24,640 --> 01:06:26,220
Everyone, close your eyes.

1827
01:06:27,760 --> 01:06:28,870
Aphid, open your eyes.

1828
01:06:29,540 --> 01:06:32,220
(This round's aphid: Confidential)

1829
01:06:32,240 --> 01:06:33,040
Start!

1830
01:06:33,120 --> 01:06:33,840
I'll go!

1831
01:06:33,840 --> 01:06:34,480
I'll go first!

1832
01:06:34,480 --> 01:06:36,640
I'm on the center platform now.

1833
01:06:36,720 --> 01:06:38,640
I'm starting the video.

1834
01:06:41,960 --> 01:06:43,120
Say something!

1835
01:06:43,120 --> 01:06:44,480
I'm...

1836
01:06:44,480 --> 01:06:45,240
Are you alone?

1837
01:06:45,240 --> 01:06:46,960
Huang Jingyu's beside me!

1838
01:06:46,960 --> 01:06:48,160
I'm protecting you!

1839
01:06:48,400 --> 01:06:49,870
I'm protecting you!

1840
01:06:50,420 --> 01:06:51,400
Okay, he's protecting me!

1841
01:06:51,400 --> 01:06:51,980
Okay!

1842
01:06:54,200 --> 01:06:55,480
Jingyu, did you open your eyes?

1843
01:06:56,340 --> 01:06:56,960
No.

1844
01:06:56,960 --> 01:06:57,540
(Eyes-closed guard)
You didn't?

1845
01:06:57,760 --> 01:06:58,720
Don't leave!

1846
01:06:58,720 --> 01:06:59,760
I'm about to write my mark!

1847
01:06:59,760 --> 01:07:00,640
I'm done!

1848
01:07:00,640 --> 01:07:01,800
Come on. I'll walk you back.

1849
01:07:01,880 --> 01:07:03,600
Okay!

1850
01:07:03,600 --> 01:07:04,520
Hu!

1851
01:07:04,520 --> 01:07:06,320
I'm back!

1852
01:07:06,400 --> 01:07:07,820
Hurry, take me back!

1853
01:07:07,820 --> 01:07:08,860
(Even the guard needs protection)

1854
01:07:08,940 --> 01:07:10,920
(Dance tasks: 1/3, aphid kills: 0/7)
My eyes are closed.

1855
01:07:11,000 --> 01:07:12,280
I'm heading over!

1856
01:07:12,480 --> 01:07:13,760
I'm coming too!

1857
01:07:13,840 --> 01:07:14,440
No need!

1858
01:07:14,440 --> 01:07:15,020
Stay there!

1859
01:07:16,240 --> 01:07:17,160
First, help me confirm

1860
01:07:17,160 --> 01:07:18,480
that I left my mark.

1861
01:07:18,560 --> 01:07:20,640
Why are there two horizontal lines?

1862
01:07:20,920 --> 01:07:22,320
One line and one slash.

1863
01:07:23,620 --> 01:07:25,740
(Anyu's acting suspicious)

1864
01:07:26,760 --> 01:07:27,180
Alarm!

1865
01:07:32,380 --> 01:07:32,860
(You're dead?)

1866
01:07:32,860 --> 01:07:34,060
(Heading back to the spawn point)

1867
01:07:41,860 --> 01:07:44,020
(This round's aphid)

1868
01:07:44,260 --> 01:07:46,340
(The aphid strikes)
I'm coming too!

1869
01:07:46,360 --> 01:07:47,790
No need! Stay there!

1870
01:07:50,620 --> 01:07:51,860
(Bai Jingting out)

1871
01:07:53,460 --> 01:07:57,100
(Everyone saw it)

1872
01:08:11,520 --> 01:08:12,440
It's Bing.

1873
01:08:12,440 --> 01:08:13,480
Bing ran this way.

1874
01:08:13,480 --> 01:08:15,180
Yeah, I saw Bing run over there.

1875
01:08:16,520 --> 01:08:18,020
But that's not who I reported.

1876
01:08:19,600 --> 01:08:20,600
Who did you report?

1877
01:08:20,600 --> 01:08:21,820
I saw Wang Anyu.

1878
01:08:22,100 --> 01:08:22,740
(Me? I'm already out)

1879
01:08:22,760 --> 01:08:24,000
Isn't he dead?

1880
01:08:24,000 --> 01:08:25,820
That's just a wolf acting cute.

1881
01:08:29,800 --> 01:08:31,360
Wang Anyu was staring at me.

1882
01:08:31,440 --> 01:08:33,560
I was scared he'd make that gesture,

1883
01:08:33,560 --> 01:08:35,040
so I yelled "alarm" first.

1884
01:08:35,040 --> 01:08:36,600
Right after I yelled, he did this!

1885
01:08:39,200 --> 01:08:40,280
I was so confused!

1886
01:08:40,800 --> 01:08:41,870
Alright, hand out the cards.

1887
01:08:44,820 --> 01:08:46,780
(New roles, fresh start)
Hand them out!

1888
01:08:46,840 --> 01:08:47,400
Seriously,

1889
01:08:47,400 --> 01:08:49,080
we can't even finish one round anymore

1890
01:08:49,080 --> 01:08:49,720
at this rate.

1891
01:08:49,720 --> 01:08:50,240
Don't laugh.

1892
01:08:50,240 --> 01:08:51,320
You can't get past round two either.

1893
01:08:51,540 --> 01:08:52,420
(Eye-contact Werewolf: secret level)

1894
01:08:52,420 --> 01:08:53,860
(Don't laugh. You can't
get past round two either. Try again)

1895
01:08:53,880 --> 01:08:55,270
Being the wolf is so hard.

1896
01:08:56,120 --> 01:08:57,750
Now everyone's scared
of drawing the wolf card.

1897
01:08:58,520 --> 01:08:59,300
Me too.

1898
01:08:59,640 --> 01:09:01,000
My heart just skipped a beat.

1899
01:09:01,680 --> 01:09:03,280
We can't even make it

1900
01:09:03,280 --> 01:09:04,560
to the discussion stage anymore!

1901
01:09:04,560 --> 01:09:04,920
True.

1902
01:09:04,920 --> 01:09:06,520
(Everyone's an expert aphid detective)
We're all like Sherlock Holmes.

1903
01:09:06,520 --> 01:09:07,160
You know?

1904
01:09:07,160 --> 01:09:08,760
But you played really well just now.

1905
01:09:08,760 --> 01:09:10,400
That eyes-closed protection was smart.

1906
01:09:10,400 --> 01:09:11,520
Right? Pretty good, huh?

1907
01:09:11,520 --> 01:09:13,760
That eyes-closed strategy was solid.

1908
01:09:13,760 --> 01:09:14,200
Wait.

1909
01:09:14,200 --> 01:09:15,720
(Security that works)
Protecting with your eyes closed?

1910
01:09:15,800 --> 01:09:16,960
Who are you protecting like that?

1911
01:09:16,960 --> 01:09:17,840
Him.

1912
01:09:18,040 --> 01:09:20,160
But you're done if someone taps you.

1913
01:09:20,160 --> 01:09:21,080
He doesn't open his eyes.

1914
01:09:21,080 --> 01:09:22,060
Tapping him won't work.

1915
01:09:24,520 --> 01:09:24,880
Come on.

1916
01:09:27,840 --> 01:09:29,520
Everyone, close your eyes.

1917
01:09:30,320 --> 01:09:31,520
Aphid, open your eyes.

1918
01:09:32,180 --> 01:09:36,060
(This round's aphid)
Everyone dreads being the wolf now.

1919
01:09:36,080 --> 01:09:37,240
(Eye-contact Werewolf)
Start!

1920
01:09:37,320 --> 01:09:39,480
(Round two begins)
I'm going up again!

1921
01:09:39,490 --> 01:09:41,240
(Claiming the center platform first)
I'm going up again!

1922
01:09:41,240 --> 01:09:41,720
I'll protect you!

1923
01:09:41,720 --> 01:09:42,260
Protect!

1924
01:09:42,260 --> 01:09:42,920
(Sticking to the bodyguard strategy)
I'll protect you!

1925
01:09:42,920 --> 01:09:43,910
Protect!

1926
01:09:44,580 --> 01:09:45,320
(Both bodyguards in position)

1927
01:09:45,320 --> 01:09:46,180
I'll protect you!

1928
01:09:47,680 --> 01:09:48,600
Starting the video!

1929
01:09:48,600 --> 01:09:49,620
So many people!

1930
01:09:49,620 --> 01:09:51,140
(The hunt begins)

1931
01:09:52,460 --> 01:09:54,820
(The dancing plants
keep their eyes shut)

1932
01:09:54,940 --> 01:09:56,340
(Looking for a dancing plant
with open eyes)

1933
01:09:56,580 --> 01:09:57,340
(Protecting)

1934
01:09:57,360 --> 01:09:58,360
Wait, he's faking the dance.

1935
01:09:58,920 --> 01:09:59,400
I really am.

1936
01:09:59,400 --> 01:10:00,840
(Danger)
These are dance steps?

1937
01:10:00,840 --> 01:10:02,620
(A professional's instinct)
Just watch the dance later!

1938
01:10:02,660 --> 01:10:04,620
(Forced to complete the task)

1939
01:10:05,620 --> 01:10:07,060
(Now that sounds right)

1940
01:10:07,080 --> 01:10:07,480
You there?

1941
01:10:07,480 --> 01:10:08,120
Everyone still here?

1942
01:10:08,120 --> 01:10:08,520
I'm here!

1943
01:10:08,520 --> 01:10:09,040
Jingyu, you there?

1944
01:10:09,040 --> 01:10:09,480
Yep!

1945
01:10:09,480 --> 01:10:10,340
I'm here!

1946
01:10:11,800 --> 01:10:13,420
(Waiting for a chance to strike)
Why's this dance so long?

1947
01:10:14,940 --> 01:10:17,060
(Nobody's opening their eyes)

1948
01:10:17,380 --> 01:10:18,740
(Forced to finish the task)
Done!

1949
01:10:18,800 --> 01:10:19,200
Let's go!

1950
01:10:19,440 --> 01:10:20,120
Hu, let's go!

1951
01:10:20,120 --> 01:10:20,640
Hold on!

1952
01:10:20,640 --> 01:10:21,540
I gotta mark this!

1953
01:10:21,820 --> 01:10:22,700
(Keeping up the act)

1954
01:10:23,520 --> 01:10:24,800
Done!

1955
01:10:24,800 --> 01:10:25,410
Heading back!

1956
01:10:26,660 --> 01:10:27,840
(Dance tasks: 1/3, aphid kills: 0/7)
Everyone here?

1957
01:10:27,840 --> 01:10:28,760
Yeah, I'm still here!

1958
01:10:28,760 --> 01:10:29,880
Here I come!

1959
01:10:29,880 --> 01:10:30,520
Protect!

1960
01:10:30,520 --> 01:10:31,360
Let's go!

1961
01:10:31,360 --> 01:10:32,860
I'm protecting you! Keep talking!

1962
01:10:32,860 --> 01:10:33,540
(Staying alert
for the aphid behind them)

1963
01:10:35,320 --> 01:10:36,440
Wang!

1964
01:10:36,440 --> 01:10:37,360
Wang's here!

1965
01:10:37,600 --> 01:10:38,720
That's our job.

1966
01:10:38,720 --> 01:10:39,920
Let's go, Iron Guards!

1967
01:10:39,920 --> 01:10:40,500
(We'll keep you safe)
Come on!

1968
01:10:41,900 --> 01:10:43,300
(Springing into action)

1969
01:10:45,140 --> 01:10:47,220
(Wang Anyu out)

1970
01:10:49,380 --> 01:10:50,100
(Quickly returning to position)

1971
01:10:50,220 --> 01:10:51,420
(Completely clueless)
Anyu?

1972
01:10:51,900 --> 01:10:52,660
(Why trust these two
to watch your back?)

1973
01:10:52,680 --> 01:10:53,600
Anyu?

1974
01:10:53,680 --> 01:10:54,840
Anyu!

1975
01:10:54,840 --> 01:10:55,840
(Pretending to be a dancing plant)
Say something!

1976
01:10:55,920 --> 01:10:56,120
Anyu?

1977
01:10:56,120 --> 01:10:57,200
(Don't scare me, Anyu!)
Something's wrong!

1978
01:10:57,280 --> 01:10:57,560
Wait!

1979
01:10:57,560 --> 01:10:58,590
Anyu!

1980
01:10:58,960 --> 01:10:59,400
Anyu?

1981
01:11:00,320 --> 01:11:00,870
Anyu!

1982
01:11:02,520 --> 01:11:02,880
Anyu?

1983
01:11:03,400 --> 01:11:03,950
Anyu!

1984
01:11:04,480 --> 01:11:05,360
Open your eyes and yell "alarm"!

1985
01:11:05,360 --> 01:11:06,600
Who's gonna call the alarm?

1986
01:11:06,600 --> 01:11:07,760
Hurry! Open your eyes and yell "alarm"!

1987
01:11:07,760 --> 01:11:08,560
Who's gonna do it?

1988
01:11:08,560 --> 01:11:09,280
Hurry! Call the alarm!

1989
01:11:09,280 --> 01:11:10,320
Alarm!

1990
01:11:10,320 --> 01:11:11,000
Churan called the alarm!

1991
01:11:11,000 --> 01:11:11,720
Hurry, call it!

1992
01:11:11,720 --> 01:11:12,720
Okay.

1993
01:11:12,720 --> 01:11:13,240
Who was it?

1994
01:11:13,240 --> 01:11:13,870
I don't know.

1995
01:11:14,800 --> 01:11:16,000
Didn't you tell me to call the alarm?

1996
01:11:20,140 --> 01:11:21,860
(Who struck while we were guarding him?)

1997
01:11:23,320 --> 01:11:23,940
Who was it?

1998
01:11:24,460 --> 01:11:25,820
(What kind of bodyguards are you two?)

1999
01:11:26,520 --> 01:11:26,960
I don't know either.

2000
01:11:26,960 --> 01:11:27,830
My eyes were closed!

2001
01:11:29,520 --> 01:11:30,360
Don't tell me it was you.

2002
01:11:30,360 --> 01:11:31,560
(The bodyguards turn on each other)
I didn't open my eyes!

2003
01:11:31,560 --> 01:11:32,960
Neither did I!

2004
01:11:33,040 --> 01:11:33,760
I was just protecting him!

2005
01:11:33,760 --> 01:11:34,810
So was I!

2006
01:11:34,810 --> 01:11:35,920
(Their security
has more holes than Swiss cheese)

2007
01:11:35,920 --> 01:11:37,080
It's a revenge killing.

2008
01:11:37,080 --> 01:11:39,060
But your hand was just on his shoulder.

2009
01:11:39,060 --> 01:11:39,880
(It was you, Fan the Bug)

2010
01:11:39,880 --> 01:11:40,320
I suspect...

2011
01:11:40,320 --> 01:11:40,960
No, I was feeling his hand

2012
01:11:40,960 --> 01:11:41,840
to see if he was dead.

2013
01:11:41,840 --> 01:11:42,840
But your hand was just

2014
01:11:42,840 --> 01:11:43,680
resting on his shoulder.

2015
01:11:43,680 --> 01:11:45,040
I think you killed him

2016
01:11:45,040 --> 01:11:46,310
and didn't pull your hand away in time!

2017
01:11:50,820 --> 01:11:52,260
(What's that supposed to mean?)

2018
01:11:52,280 --> 01:11:53,280
Was it you?

2019
01:11:53,280 --> 01:11:53,880
Finally!

2020
01:11:53,880 --> 01:11:55,380
(Requesting a trial)
We actually get to discuss things!

2021
01:11:56,600 --> 01:11:57,200
Come on!

2022
01:11:57,200 --> 01:11:58,240
Sit down!

2023
01:11:58,720 --> 01:11:59,660
Let's figure this out!

2024
01:11:59,660 --> 01:12:00,380
(Finally made it past round one)

2025
01:12:00,460 --> 01:12:01,140
(A rare first-round discussion)

2026
01:12:01,140 --> 01:12:01,740
(Dance tasks: 1/3, aphid kills: 1/7)

2027
01:12:01,760 --> 01:12:02,240
Well

2028
01:12:02,240 --> 01:12:03,120
it's one of you two.

2029
01:12:03,120 --> 01:12:04,920
I really kept my eyes closed
the whole time.

2030
01:12:04,920 --> 01:12:05,440
Me too.

2031
01:12:05,440 --> 01:12:06,520
How'd Hu survive?

2032
01:12:06,520 --> 01:12:07,640
I think the chances of us being the wolf

2033
01:12:07,640 --> 01:12:08,920
are pretty slim.

2034
01:12:09,280 --> 01:12:11,080
That proves our protection worked.

2035
01:12:11,080 --> 01:12:12,240
Then, Wang Anyu,

2036
01:12:12,240 --> 01:12:13,520
what were you showing off for?

2037
01:12:13,520 --> 01:12:14,380
(Stereotype confirmed)
You got yourself killed.

2038
01:12:15,520 --> 01:12:17,160
We took the exact same route

2039
01:12:17,160 --> 01:12:18,520
with the same protection.

2040
01:12:18,520 --> 01:12:19,880
So how come Hu...

2041
01:12:19,960 --> 01:12:21,260
So you're blaming me?

2042
01:12:22,740 --> 01:12:24,140
(Just asking. Don't get mad)

2043
01:12:26,080 --> 01:12:28,420
(Putting out the fire)
Hu made it back in one piece!

2044
01:12:28,600 --> 01:12:29,860
Did you turn around or something?

2045
01:12:29,940 --> 01:12:31,180
(Still provoking him)

2046
01:12:33,560 --> 01:12:34,960
Just wait till I'm allowed
to talk again!

2047
01:12:34,960 --> 01:12:35,760
Just you wait!

2048
01:12:35,760 --> 01:12:36,720
I'll give you an earful!

2049
01:12:36,720 --> 01:12:39,060
I think he's fuming!

2050
01:12:42,620 --> 01:12:43,740
(Who should I frame?)

2051
01:12:43,760 --> 01:12:44,240
Wait.

2052
01:12:44,240 --> 01:12:45,360
Just because I survived

2053
01:12:45,360 --> 01:12:47,500
doesn't mean you two
are definitely innocent.

2054
01:12:47,500 --> 01:12:49,180
(Either one works for me)

2055
01:12:51,160 --> 01:12:51,680
I think

2056
01:12:51,680 --> 01:12:52,720
it's one of you two.

2057
01:12:55,380 --> 01:12:56,780
(Churan will defend me)

2058
01:12:56,810 --> 01:12:58,470
Easy there, or he'll get you!

2059
01:13:01,140 --> 01:13:02,360
(Her aphid side is showing)
I really am.

2060
01:13:02,900 --> 01:13:04,660
(You've been paralyzed)

2061
01:13:04,880 --> 01:13:06,470
Then you're really good at this game.

2062
01:13:06,740 --> 01:13:08,260
(What's that supposed to mean?)

2063
01:13:08,520 --> 01:13:09,980
Roll your eyes back
and you can't see him.

2064
01:13:15,240 --> 01:13:17,450
You even dance
with your eyes rolled back!

2065
01:13:20,600 --> 01:13:22,040
Let's split into two rows.

2066
01:13:22,040 --> 01:13:23,230
One row up there.

2067
01:13:27,760 --> 01:13:29,340
I didn't hear anyone moving this round.

2068
01:13:29,920 --> 01:13:30,400
Hear?

2069
01:13:30,400 --> 01:13:31,720
We were shouting over each other!

2070
01:13:31,720 --> 01:13:32,520
How could you hear anyone moving?

2071
01:13:32,520 --> 01:13:33,160
I can vouch for you.

2072
01:13:33,840 --> 01:13:34,920
I'll vouch for you. You vouch for me.

2073
01:13:34,920 --> 01:13:35,480
I'll vouch for you.

2074
01:13:36,020 --> 01:13:37,700
(Just one question)

2075
01:13:37,720 --> 01:13:40,440
He could vouch for you if he's the wolf.

2076
01:13:40,440 --> 01:13:42,260
But how can you vouch for him?

2077
01:13:42,260 --> 01:13:46,300
(Brain completely short-circuited)

2078
01:13:48,690 --> 01:13:50,160
Neither of you opened your eyes?

2079
01:13:50,400 --> 01:13:51,600
Nope.

2080
01:13:51,600 --> 01:13:53,700
(One more question)
Then how do you know he didn't?

2081
01:13:53,740 --> 01:13:58,420
(Brain short-circuits again)

2082
01:14:02,240 --> 01:14:02,760
No, wait.

2083
01:14:04,040 --> 01:14:04,880
Don't let them fool you.

2084
01:14:04,880 --> 01:14:06,800
I really didn't open my eyes.

2085
01:14:06,860 --> 01:14:08,940
(Stirring up more confusion)

2086
01:14:08,960 --> 01:14:10,680
After you asked him that,

2087
01:14:10,680 --> 01:14:12,560
it was like all his strength

2088
01:14:12,560 --> 01:14:14,140
just drained away!

2089
01:14:14,260 --> 01:14:16,020
(That really got to him)

2090
01:14:18,240 --> 01:14:20,040
It's suspicious
that he's fixated on that.

2091
01:14:20,040 --> 01:14:20,980
Very suspicious.

2092
01:14:20,980 --> 01:14:21,710
Oh my God!

2093
01:14:21,710 --> 01:14:23,580
Can't I ask for a little logic?

2094
01:14:24,040 --> 01:14:25,240
If we wanted to kill someone,

2095
01:14:25,240 --> 01:14:26,490
Hu wouldn't have survived.

2096
01:14:27,960 --> 01:14:28,800
Since Hu made it back alive,

2097
01:14:28,800 --> 01:14:29,920
maybe Hu's the wolf.

2098
01:14:34,320 --> 01:14:35,060
Hu?

2099
01:14:35,600 --> 01:14:37,600
It's possible.

2100
01:14:37,600 --> 01:14:38,840
(Panicking)
After we protected him,

2101
01:14:39,600 --> 01:14:40,360
nobody went after him

2102
01:14:40,360 --> 01:14:41,150
or tried to kill him.

2103
01:14:41,800 --> 01:14:43,800
You two were standing there
like idiots,

2104
01:14:43,880 --> 01:14:44,880
saying, "I'll protect him!"

2105
01:14:44,960 --> 01:14:47,150
Meanwhile, he was opening
his eyes and killing everyone!

2106
01:14:48,540 --> 01:14:49,600
That's possible, right?

2107
01:14:49,600 --> 01:14:50,160
Isn't it?

2108
01:14:50,160 --> 01:14:51,360
- It's possible.
- It is.

2109
01:14:51,560 --> 01:14:53,240
Then why would he bother doing the task?

2110
01:14:53,840 --> 01:14:55,400
Why wouldn't I just wait to kill people?

2111
01:14:55,880 --> 01:14:57,060
Did anyone check the paper?

2112
01:14:57,060 --> 01:14:58,700
(But who can prove
he's telling the truth?)

2113
01:15:00,760 --> 01:15:01,420
I did.

2114
01:15:02,400 --> 01:15:02,720
You did?

2115
01:15:02,720 --> 01:15:03,570
When did you look?

2116
01:15:06,020 --> 01:15:07,340
(I'm back in the game)

2117
01:15:08,680 --> 01:15:10,240
Huang Jingyu,

2118
01:15:10,320 --> 01:15:11,520
how'd you see it?

2119
01:15:11,640 --> 01:15:12,600
You checked the paper?

2120
01:15:12,600 --> 01:15:14,400
Didn't you say your eyes
were closed the whole time?

2121
01:15:14,480 --> 01:15:16,060
I checked when I stepped down.

2122
01:15:16,880 --> 01:15:17,880
What are you laughing at?

2123
01:15:17,880 --> 01:15:18,840
Answer properly!

2124
01:15:19,840 --> 01:15:21,540
I can't even laugh now?

2125
01:15:22,830 --> 01:15:24,000
In this game,

2126
01:15:24,000 --> 01:15:25,360
you can't just laugh whenever you want.

2127
01:15:25,600 --> 01:15:27,880
(Still don't get it?)
Your killer side's showing!

2128
01:15:27,880 --> 01:15:28,720
No, wait!

2129
01:15:30,720 --> 01:15:31,850
I've just been

2130
01:15:32,640 --> 01:15:34,650
working as a bodyguard here.

2131
01:15:35,680 --> 01:15:36,580
I suspect Jingyu

2132
01:15:37,480 --> 01:15:38,960
because he's acting weird this round.

2133
01:15:39,520 --> 01:15:40,470
When isn't he weird?

2134
01:15:44,690 --> 01:15:46,050
Has he ever acted normal?

2135
01:15:50,440 --> 01:15:52,600
But the way Jingyu laughed earlier,

2136
01:15:52,600 --> 01:15:54,840
I just don't get it.

2137
01:15:54,840 --> 01:15:57,120
It sounded like he'd
accidentally exposed himself!

2138
01:15:57,280 --> 01:15:58,620
I just thought it was funny.

2139
01:15:58,940 --> 01:16:00,560
(Naturally cheerful)
But Jingyu's definitely not the wolf.

2140
01:16:01,600 --> 01:16:02,370
How do you know?

2141
01:16:04,850 --> 01:16:06,240
Can't I trust my gut?

2142
01:16:07,810 --> 01:16:08,600
You...

2143
01:16:08,600 --> 01:16:09,360
All these years,

2144
01:16:09,360 --> 01:16:11,280
you've never pulled this before!

2145
01:16:11,280 --> 01:16:12,370
Suddenly trusting your gut?

2146
01:16:12,370 --> 01:16:13,000
No.

2147
01:16:13,000 --> 01:16:14,480
I've got my reasoning,

2148
01:16:14,480 --> 01:16:15,480
and I've got my gut feeling.

2149
01:16:15,480 --> 01:16:16,090
He's definitely not the wolf.

2150
01:16:22,840 --> 01:16:24,280
Bai's acting weird this round too.

2151
01:16:24,280 --> 01:16:26,420
(Plenty of weirdos here)
He hasn't made a sound.

2152
01:16:29,240 --> 01:16:29,840
That's

2153
01:16:29,840 --> 01:16:31,350
suspicious now too?

2154
01:16:33,990 --> 01:16:34,640
Alright.

2155
01:16:34,640 --> 01:16:35,660
Let's vote Bai out first.

2156
01:16:35,810 --> 01:16:36,720
Where...

2157
01:16:36,720 --> 01:16:37,840
Where'd that accusation come from?

2158
01:16:37,840 --> 01:16:38,720
You're voting me out?

2159
01:16:38,720 --> 01:16:39,720
I didn't even move!

2160
01:16:39,900 --> 01:16:41,190
Then why were you so quiet?

2161
01:16:42,640 --> 01:16:43,280
What's your problem?

2162
01:16:43,280 --> 01:16:44,080
I saw nothing! My eyes were closed!

2163
01:16:44,080 --> 01:16:44,800
He's an introvert.

2164
01:16:44,800 --> 01:16:46,200
Can an introvert act like that?

2165
01:16:46,200 --> 01:16:46,960
My eyes were closed!

2166
01:16:46,960 --> 01:16:48,080
I didn't see anything!

2167
01:16:48,080 --> 01:16:48,600
I...

2168
01:16:48,600 --> 01:16:49,420
What could I even say?

2169
01:16:49,960 --> 01:16:50,960
But I was quiet too.

2170
01:16:53,150 --> 01:16:53,710
Then let's vote you out.

2171
01:16:55,570 --> 01:16:56,480
Say that again.

2172
01:16:57,680 --> 01:16:58,290
Vote him out.

2173
01:16:59,060 --> 01:17:00,280
You've already got two votes.

2174
01:17:02,450 --> 01:17:03,540
And you're still provoking me?

2175
01:17:04,440 --> 01:17:04,830
Three votes.

2176
01:17:05,620 --> 01:17:07,030
But I'm really innocent.

2177
01:17:07,760 --> 01:17:09,100
Like that's convincing.

2178
01:17:10,600 --> 01:17:11,280
It's Chengcheng.

2179
01:17:11,280 --> 01:17:12,470
I think it's definitely Chengcheng.

2180
01:17:13,480 --> 01:17:14,070
Let's vote.

2181
01:17:15,080 --> 01:17:16,080
You're so quick to judge!

2182
01:17:16,080 --> 01:17:17,480
Now I'll have

2183
01:17:17,480 --> 01:17:18,920
to watch out for him.

2184
01:17:18,920 --> 01:17:20,000
I'm willing to die.

2185
01:17:20,000 --> 01:17:20,880
(Sacrificing himself for the team)
Okay?

2186
01:17:20,880 --> 01:17:21,510
Die then!

2187
01:17:24,240 --> 01:17:25,090
Dancing plant!

2188
01:17:26,040 --> 01:17:27,460
You paralyzed me.

2189
01:17:29,600 --> 01:17:31,320
I have a feeling
it's not Fan Chengcheng,

2190
01:17:31,320 --> 01:17:32,840
but I have to vote him out.

2191
01:17:35,760 --> 01:17:37,520
Why don't we hold off a little?

2192
01:17:37,600 --> 01:17:39,470
Then what's your theory?

2193
01:17:40,920 --> 01:17:41,960
I guess I'll

2194
01:17:41,960 --> 01:17:43,100
have to trust my gut now.

2195
01:17:43,340 --> 01:17:44,700
(Secretly delighted)

2196
01:17:44,720 --> 01:17:47,240
As one of the good guys,

2197
01:17:47,240 --> 01:17:48,680
I already kept Hu safe once.

2198
01:17:48,680 --> 01:17:49,800
So I think

2199
01:17:51,000 --> 01:17:51,840
maybe you could

2200
01:17:51,840 --> 01:17:52,840
spare me this time.

2201
01:17:52,840 --> 01:17:54,440
I can still help next round.

2202
01:17:54,440 --> 01:17:55,430
I can call the alarm.

2203
01:17:58,180 --> 01:17:59,140
(Who should we vote for?)

2204
01:17:59,160 --> 01:17:59,630
Vote.

2205
01:18:01,460 --> 01:18:03,500
(Wang Churan x1,
Fan Chengcheng x4, abstained x2)

2206
01:18:03,520 --> 01:18:04,540
Six.

2207
01:18:04,540 --> 01:18:05,300
(Fan Chengcheng out)

2208
01:18:06,840 --> 01:18:08,480
It was nice working with you.

2209
01:18:08,480 --> 01:18:09,900
I can't be captain anymore?

2210
01:18:10,020 --> 01:18:11,380
(The bodyguard duo breaks up)

2211
01:18:11,400 --> 01:18:12,540
The security team's disbanded?

2212
01:18:13,760 --> 01:18:14,820
Wait, it really wasn't you?

2213
01:18:15,600 --> 01:18:16,640
Alright, let's continue.

2214
01:18:16,640 --> 01:18:16,920
Continue?

2215
01:18:16,920 --> 01:18:17,980
So it wasn't him.

2216
01:18:18,420 --> 01:18:20,620
(Who made it past round two?)

2217
01:18:20,660 --> 01:18:22,100
(Hu's got some tricks up his sleeve)

2218
01:18:22,180 --> 01:18:23,260
(An aphid has made it to round two!)

2219
01:18:23,280 --> 01:18:24,840
A huge bug!

2220
01:18:24,920 --> 01:18:26,220
A huge bug!

2221
01:18:26,300 --> 01:18:27,420
Get it away!

2222
01:18:29,880 --> 01:18:30,580
Is it gone?

2223
01:18:32,800 --> 01:18:33,280
What...

